From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:31:21 +0200
Subject: nv30: point sizes from the vertex program (POINT_PARAMETERS_ENABLE)

Yamagi Quake II's gl1 particles (gl1_pointparameters 1) were round discs of one size at every
distance on the PS3, about 40 pixels where the PC draws them a few pixels wide far away
(2026-10-27). The game sets glPointSize 40 (times the height / 480), GL_POINT_SIZE_MIN/MAX 2/40
and GL_POINT_DISTANCE_ATTENUATION (0.01, 0, 0.01); Mesa's fixed-function vertex program then
writes the attenuated, clamped size to PSIZ, nvfx puts it in the PSZ output and NV40's
VP_RESULT_EN has its bit, and the state tracker sets point_size_per_vertex. But nv30 never set
POINT_PARAMETERS_ENABLE (0x1ee4, libgcm's NV4097_SET_POINT_PARAMS_ENABLE), and ps3fb's init leaves
it 0, so the RSX took POINT_SIZE, the glPointSize, for every point: gl_PointSize and
GL_VERTEX_PROGRAM_POINT_SIZE were ignored the same way.

The rasterizer state now sets it from point_size_per_vertex. On the PS3 only when ps3rsx's
PS3_ABI getparam is 2 or more: ps3rsx 1 rejects the method (its validator's allowlist), and a
rejected push is lost, so this Mesa on an older module keeps the old sizes instead.

Checked on the RSX (ps3rsx with PS3_ABI 2) with ps3-gpu-tools' gl-pointsmooth, its two
attenuation rows (Quake II's settings, eye distances 0 to 200: sizes 40 down to 2): every point
40 pixels before, 40, 19, 9, 7, 3, 2 after (llvmpipe 40, 20, 10, 8, 4, 2: the RSX drops the
fraction of a per-vertex size, and these are 19.98, 9.997, 7.998, 3.9998). With ps3rsx 1 the
old sizes and no rejected push. In Quake II's demo the particles are small far away and big
near, as on the PC.

Found by: gamedb:yquake2 (investigations/2026-10-27-point-size-attenuation)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.c
@@ -334,6 +334,7 @@ nouveau_screen_init(struct nouveau_screen *screen, struct nouveau_device *dev)
                     !nouveau_getparam(dev, NOUVEAU_GETPARAM_PCI_VENDOR, &vendor) &&
                     vendor == 0x104d &&
                     !nouveau_getparam(dev, 0x1000 /* PS3_ABI */, &ps3_abi);
+   screen->ps3_abi = screen->is_ps3 ? ps3_abi : 0;
    screen->ps3_relocs = screen->is_ps3 && debug_get_bool_option("NV30_PS3_RELOCS", false);
    if (screen->is_ps3) {
       nv04_data.vram = 0xfeed0000;
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.h b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nouveau_screen.h
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@ struct nouveau_screen {
    bool is_uma;
    bool disable_fences;
    bool is_ps3; /* RSX behind the ps3rsx kernel driver: PS3 handles and offsets */
+   uint64_t ps3_abi; /* its PS3_ABI getparam: 2 and up take POINT_PARAMS_ENABLE (0x1ee4) */
    bool ps3_relocs; /* NV30_PS3_RELOCS: send relocations on the PS3 too (as before 0019) */
    void *svm_cutout;
    size_t svm_cutout_size;
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state.c b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state.c
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state.c
@@ -134,6 +134,7 @@ static void *
 nv30_rasterizer_state_create(struct pipe_context *pipe,
                              const struct pipe_rasterizer_state *cso)
 {
+   struct nouveau_screen *screen = &nv30_context(pipe)->screen->base;
    struct nv30_rasterizer_stateobj *so;
 
    so = CALLOC_STRUCT(nv30_rasterizer_stateobj);
@@ -184,6 +185,14 @@ nv30_rasterizer_state_create(struct pipe_context *pipe,
    SB_DATA  (so, cso->poly_stipple_enable);
    SB_MTHD30(so, POINT_SIZE, 1);
    SB_DATA  (so, fui(cso->point_size));
+   /* The point size from the vertex program's PSZ output (GL_POINT_DISTANCE_ATTENUATION,
+    * gl_PointSize) instead of POINT_SIZE: without it the RSX drew every such point at the
+    * glPointSize. Not on a ps3rsx whose validator rejects the method (PS3_ABI 1).
+    */
+   if (!screen->is_ps3 || screen->ps3_abi >= 2) {
+      SB_MTHD30(so, POINT_PARAMETERS_ENABLE, 1);
+      SB_DATA  (so, cso->point_size_per_vertex);
+   }
    SB_MTHD30(so, FLATSHADE_FIRST, 1);
    SB_DATA  (so, cso->flatshade_first);
 
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state.h b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state.h
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state.h
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/nouveau/nv30/nv30_state.h
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ struct nv30_blend_stateobj {
 
 struct nv30_rasterizer_stateobj {
    struct pipe_rasterizer_state pipe;
-   unsigned data[32];
+   unsigned data[36];
    unsigned size;
 };
 
